  "hindi": "वह उसके लिए पूरी तरह समर्थ है: पहले, वह दूसरे, और तीसरे के रूप में भी; वह मनुष्य का होता है। दूसरी का गर्भ दूसरों ने उत्पन्न किया; वह श्रेष्ठ वृषभ दूसरों के साथ रहता है।",
  "english": "He is fully sufficient for him: first, he second, and also third; he is the Hotṛ priest of man. Others begot the embryo of another; he, the noble bull, keeps company with others.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Unclear verse; literal rendering only. sāsmā read as sa + asmai (see 2.17.6); 'is fully sufficient' supplies the verb for aram; prathamam, dvitīyam, tṛtīyam taken as adverbial 'first, second, third'. manuṣaḥ 'of man' (or 'of Manu'). anyasyāḥ garbham: 'embryo' is literal, the referent is not stated; jenya 'noble' (or 'genuine'). The subject (he) is not named.",
