  "hindi": "अब मैं इन्द्र के दोनों भूरे-पीले घोड़ों को रथ में जोड़ूँगा, उसके आने के लिए, नए सुकथित वचन के साथ। बहुत से प्रेरित कवि यहाँ तुझे न रोकें, और दूसरे यजमान भी नहीं।",
  "english": "Now I will yoke the two tawny horses of Indra to the chariot, with a new, well-spoken word, for his coming. Let not the inspired poets, indeed many, nor other sacrificers, hold you back here.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "ratha is rathe (e + i -> a i); rathe read as 'to/in the chariot'. kam (nu kam) is an emphasising particle. mo ṣu = mā u su. ni rīraman taken as a prohibitive aorist injunctive 'let them not detain'. The speaker addresses Indra in the second half (tvām), having spoken of him in the third person in the first half.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "type": "verse",
